WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.018
Coevo Caddie.

2
00:00:02.018 --> 00:00:05.150
A coach on the phone beside your screen.

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.103
A café owner is making a dessert poster with Meta AI.

4
00:00:11.103 --> 00:00:15.407
It looks generic, so they type: make it more premium.

5
00:00:15.407 --> 00:00:16.300
Then again.

6
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.189
Setup is four steps.

7
00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:25.774
Open the Desk on your computer, and scan its code with your phone.

8
00:00:25.774 --> 00:00:29.455
Aim the phone at your screen, and tap Start watching.

9
00:00:29.455 --> 00:00:31.400
Then keep working, as usual.

10
00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:38.748
The Caddie watches quietly, and says why it stays quiet.

11
00:00:38.748 --> 00:00:42.537
After the third, more premium, it asks one question.

12
00:00:42.537 --> 00:00:44.942
What exactly is your new dessert?

13
00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.636
The owner answers out loud.

14
00:00:50.636 --> 00:00:55.014
The Caddie hears matcha, but the poster still shows berries.

15
00:00:55.014 --> 00:01:00.267
So it names what is missing: the price, a real photo, and who it is for.

16
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.061
Now the owner writes a real brief.

17
00:01:05.061 --> 00:01:11.117
The poster shows the dessert and its price, and the change is marked: with the Caddie.

18
00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:18.586
Afterwards, it keeps only what the session earned.

19
00:01:18.586 --> 00:01:22.809
A note, a playbook, flashcards for later, and a short video.

20
00:01:22.809 --> 00:01:26.117
This time it skipped the podcast, and said why.

21
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:33.050
From an earlier recorded run: a two-voice podcast, and a vertical short.

22
00:01:33.475 --> 00:01:38.075
Podcast guest (Mina): “What did you actually write? Give me the exact line, not theory.”

23
00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:44.170
Podcast, the Caddie: “You wrote, ‘The new dessert is matcha basque cheesecake, priced at KRW 6,500.’”

24
00:01:44.885 --> 00:01:47.940
Short: “What happens when you ask for premium three times without a brief?”

25
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.249
In the Practice Range, you brief a new request.

26
00:01:53.249 --> 00:02:00.025
Muse Image draws what your words produce, and the Caddie checks which details your brief includes.

27
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.446
Your AI learns too.

28
00:02:03.446 --> 00:02:05.500
The Caddie proposes a card.

29
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.675
You approve it, and pin it as the first message of a dedicated chat.

30
00:02:11.867 --> 00:02:18.824
In a separate check, asked for a new drink poster, Meta AI asked those five questions first.

31
00:02:18.824 --> 00:02:20.942
And the Caddie stayed quiet.

32
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.636
Four Meta models.

33
00:02:23.636 --> 00:02:26.428
Muse Spark reads and decides.

34
00:02:26.428 --> 00:02:27.872
SAM 3.1 points.

35
00:02:27.872 --> 00:02:30.279
Voice Transcribe listens.

36
00:02:30.279 --> 00:02:32.300
And Muse Image draws.

37
00:02:34.333 --> 00:02:35.410
Keep your AI.

38
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:40.333 line:5%
[On screen] Coevo Caddie app: newly implemented during this hackathon. Based on my earlier Coevo concept.

39
00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:38.226
And add a caddie, right beside it.

40
00:02:38.226 --> 00:02:39.633
Try Coevo Caddie.
